  "interpretation": {
    "direct3d": "Sparse primitive SigLIP/MPR improves Ramen direct-3D selection substantially over no sparse regularization. Dense rendered SigLIP/text loss does not substitute for sparse primitive supervision and reduces the sparse-only direct3D result in this short-finetune setting.",
    "rendered2d": "Rendered-view performance remains strong without dense SigLIP/text loss. Sparse primitive regularization at the tested weight creates a 2D tradeoff, so the final method should keep sparse primitive semantic regularization controlled or staged instead of presenting SigLIP as a dense rendered reconstruction loss.",
    "paper_story": "The ablation supports separating dense rendered RADIO/structural reconstruction from sparse primitive semantic usability regularization. SigLIP should be described as a sparse primitive semantic anchor in MPR, while dense SAM/DINO-style structural signals belong to rendered-view feature reconstruction/regularization."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Single-scene Ramen ablation.",
    "Short 8-epoch finetune from an existing warmstart.",
    "Direct3D uses best threshold over a global threshold sweep because short-finetune checkpoints are not calibrated for the final promoted thr0p65 setting.",
    "This artifact validates directionality and wording, not final four-scene leaderboard numbers."
  ]
